# HopOn Netherlands

HopOn is a mobile-first guide to places in Amsterdam, Rotterdam and Utrecht. Search and filter the curated OpenStreetMap catalog, explore it on a MapLibre map, discover nearby mobility hubs, and use Discover by Vibe to shape a day around selected places.

## Plans

Choose between 1 and 12 unique places from one city to create a plan. A new plan remains a temporary draft in that browser tab's `sessionStorage` until it is saved. Saved Plans are stored by the Spring API in in-memory H2 and support the full Create → List → Read → Update → Delete flow. Saved plans survive page refreshes while the backend process is running; they reset when that process restarts.

The API used by the plans screens is:

| Request | Success response |
| --- | --- |
| `POST /api/plans` | `201 Created` with a `Location` header |
| `GET /api/plans` | `200 OK` |
| `GET /api/plans/{id}` | `200 OK`, or `404 Not Found` |
| `PUT /api/plans/{id}` | `200 OK` |
| `DELETE /api/plans/{id}` | `204 No Content`, or `404 Not Found` |

## Run locally (Windows PowerShell)

Terminal 1, from the repository root:

```powershell
.\.tools\run-backend.ps1
```

This starts the Java 27 / Spring Boot API at `http://localhost:8080` using the Gradle 9.8.2 wrapper.

Terminal 2, from the repository root:

```powershell
cd frontend
npm ci
npm start
```

Use a Node.js version matching `^22.22.3 || ^24.15.0 || ^26.0.0` from `frontend/package.json`. Open `http://localhost:4200`. Angular proxies `/api/**` to the backend. `npm run start:lan` serves the UI on the local network.

## Checks

Backend tests and executable archive (PowerShell, from the repository root):

```powershell
cd backend
.\gradlew.bat clean test bootJar
```

Frontend checks (PowerShell, from the repository root):

```powershell
cd frontend
npm ci
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test
npm run build
```

For browser E2E, first start the backend with `.\.tools\run-backend.ps1` from the repository root in a separate terminal. Then, from `frontend/`, install Chromium once and run the browser suite:

```powershell
cd frontend
npx playwright install chromium
npm run test:e2e
```

Playwright starts a separate Angular server on port 4300 and proxies API requests to the running Spring backend at port 8080.

The city catalog is a static OpenStreetMap snapshot. Map styles and tiles require a network connection; browsing and saved-plan CRUD remain available when map tiles cannot load.
